Jim is, I think, correct, to the extent that if the community melted
away (in favour of another fork, or another roguelike, or just Away),
the DevTeam would most likely give development of NH up as a bad
job. (They might tell themselves that they intended to carry on, but I
think that without the motivation of people wanting to play their game
they'd never actually get to the point of releasing anything.)

However, there's little sign of that happening; and it has little
bearing on the question of whether there's critical mass to support
non-DevTeam development efforts at all. All I hear at present is a few
impatient voices.

(And the idea of any such effort being called NetHack is, I think, a
non-starter; regardless of what it may choose to call _itself_, it'll
be given a different name by the community for distinguishing
purposes.)

